", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout is mixed: us-east is on v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. I'll retry the same rollback to v2.3.0 to finish it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UMuouvYBoQfF8L4cipA8gC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014puZy8KYUcoZcXuii4Mp6P", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "All three regions are now on v2.3.0 and healthy. Next I'll open the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016h4D15jgm5DdaQseigccJ8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.2.9 and v2.3.0 were healthy; v2.3.1 unhealthy; v2.3.1-rc was staging-only and unhealthy). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial failure, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west, and eu-west, healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until root cause is fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025-incident-1"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. Because I used an idempotency key, retrying with the same key will not create a duplicate, so I'll retry.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01RytuR4gYRdna7n1yBb7TWn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.2.9 and v2.3.0 were healthy; v2.3.1 unhealthy; v2.3.1-rc was staging-only and unhealthy). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial failure, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west, and eu-west, healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until root cause is fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025-incident-1"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 was unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc had only run in staging.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed. I retried the same rollback, and it completed. checkout-api now reports v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, healthy, with error rate 0.002 (down from 0.18).\n- **Incident:** The first incident request timed out. I retried with the same idempotency key, and the incident was created once. The summary records the actions above and the partial failure, and recommends not redeploying v2.3.1 until its root cause is fixed.\n\nThe orchestrator partial failure during the first rollback attempt still needs follow-up, and the incident is the place to track it.", "type": "text"}]}]}